<p> Mining			92.7   92.9   90.7   91.9   89.3</p>
<p> Utilities		   91.6   91.4   90.0   92.6   90.7</p>
<p>Wall Street economists were expecting a 0.1 percent rise in September industrial production and an 83.3 percent capacity use rate.</p>
<p>Motor vehicle assemblies fell in September to a rate of 6.5 million a year for automobiles from 6.7 million in August. For light trucks the assembly rate was down to 5.4 million in September from 5.6 million in August.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles and parts, September industrial output rose 0.4 percent after rising 0.5 percent in August.</p>
<p>For the third quarter, growth in industrial output slowed to an annual rate of 4.4 percent from 6.7 percent in the second quarter, the Fed said. It added the slowing was evident in most major market groups except nondurable consumer goods and durable goods materials.</p>
